    "title": "LEGION BASEBALL: Hawks sweep Torrington on the road | Cheyenne Post 6 | wyomingnews.com",
    "text": "CHEYENNE – Three runs in the fifth inning gave the Cheyenne Hawks enough breathing room to pick up a 4-0 win over the Torrington Tigers during the first half of the doubleheader Wednesday in Torrington.\nNolan Gorman led the Hawks from the plate, going 2-for-4 with a double and one RBI. Chase Aragon, Will Shaw and Kellin Wenzel added hits, as well.\nAlex Vines pitched 5⅔ innings, allowing three hits and four walks while striking out 11 batters.\nThe Hawks led 7-0 going into the third inning of the second game before Torrington rattled off four runs to cut the lead to three. After a scoreless fourth, Cheyenne put seven runs across in the fifth inning to put the game away for a 14-5 win.\nGorman led the team with a 3-for-4 clip from the plate. Troy Nelson had a double and team-best three RBI. Wenzel, Shaw, Than Hardy and Ayden Gamo had two hits each. Hardy also pitched five innings, allowing four hits and three walks. Of his five runs against, only one of them was earned.",
